              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong bicategory
            is a particular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+definition+of+higher+category"} algebraic
            notion of
            %em
              weak
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            (in fact, the earliest to be formulated, and still the one in most common use). The idea is that a bicategory is a category
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+enrichment"} weakly enriched
            over
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-objects"} hom-objects
            of a bicategory are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-category"} hom-categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched categories
            hold only up to coherent isomorphism.
          %p
            For information on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            of bicategories, see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctor"} pseudofunctor
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong bicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            consists of
          %ul
            %li
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/collection"} collection
              of
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y,z,\dots
              = succeed ";" do
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                  \-cells
            %li
              For each pair of
              = succeed "-cells" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(x,y)
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              or
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                \-cells
              and whose morphisms are called
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphisms"} 2-morphisms
              or
              = succeed ";" do
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
                  \-cells
            %li
              For each
              = succeed "-cell" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              = succeed "-cell" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_x\in B(x,x)
              called the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity morphism
              or
              %strong
                identity
                = succeed "-cell" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              at
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %li
              For each triple of
              = succeed "-cells" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y,z
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\circ}\colon B(y,z)\times B(x,y) \to B(x,z)
              called
              = succeed ";" do
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+composition"} horizontal composition
            %li
              For each pair of
              = succeed "-cells" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural isomorphisms
              called
              = succeed ":" do
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitors"} unitors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right center left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mi f
                            %mo ∘
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mi x
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi θ
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mi θ
                            %mo ∘
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mi x
                      %mo )
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right center left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mi y
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi θ
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mi y
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi θ
                      %mo )
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    \\begin{array}{rcl}
                    f&amp;\mapsto&amp;f \circ 1_x\\
                    \\theta&amp;\mapsto&amp;\theta \circ 1_{1_x}
                    \\end{array}
                    \\right)  \cong id_{B(x,y)} \cong \left(
                    \\begin{array}{rcl}
                    f&amp;\mapsto&amp;1_y\circ f\\
                    \\theta&amp;\mapsto&amp;1_{1_y} \circ \theta
                    \\end{array}
                    \\right):B(x,y)\rightarrow B(x,y)
            %li
              For each quadruple of
              = succeed "-cells" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w,x,y,z
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associator"} associator
              between the two functors from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(y,z) \times B(x,y) \times B(w,x)
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(w,z)
              built out of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\circ}
          %p such that
          %ul
            %li
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pentagon+identity"} pentagon identity
              is satisfied by the
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associators"} associators
            %li
              And the triangle identity is satisfied by the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitors"} unitors
          %p
            If there is exactly one
            = succeed "-cell," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(*,*)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping+hypothesis"} delooping hypothesis
            and the general notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-tuply+monoidal+n-category"} k-tuply monoidal n-category
          %h3#detailedDefn Details
          %p
            Here we spell out the above definition in full detail. Compare to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category#detailedDefn"}
                detailed definition of strict
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
          %p
            A bicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            consists of
          %ul
            %li
              a collection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ob
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ob B
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ob
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ob_B
              of
              %em objects
              or
