                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B M
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
                (see there).
            %li
              %p
                Categories,
                = succeed "s," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor"} anafunctor
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
                in the absence of the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anabicategory"} anabicategory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"}> Rings
                ,
                = succeed "s," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodule"} bimodule
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched categories
            %li
              %p
                Objects,
                = succeed "s," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+2-groupoid"} fundamental 2-groupoid
                of a space is a bicategory which is not necessarily strict (although it can be made strict fairly easily when the space is Hausdorff by quotienting by
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thin+homotopy"} thin homotopy
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+groupoid"} path groupoid
                and
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+infinity-groupoid"} fundamental infinity-groupoid
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complex"} crossed complex
          %h2#Coherence Coherence theorems
          %p
            One way to state the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence+theorem"} coherence theorem
            for bicategories is that every bicategory is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+2-categories"} equivalent
            to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"} strict 2-category
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rectification"} rectification
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            to be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associators"} associators
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitors"} unitors
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commutes
          %p
            Note that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=2
            is the greatest value of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            for which every weak
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-strict+infinity-category"} semi-strict infinity-category
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gray-category"} Gray-category
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof"} proof
            of the coherence theorem is basically the same as the proof of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence+theorem+for+monoidal+categories"} coherence theorem for monoidal categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Power89"} Power 1989
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lack%27s+coherence+theorem"} Lack's coherence theorem
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rectification"} rectification
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategories"} bicategories
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-categories"} strict 2-categories
            can be expressed in terms of a
            %span.newWikiWord
              triadjunction
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/triadjunction"} ?
            between
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tricategories"} tricategories
            = succeed "." do
